    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 12,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "A coil carries a high frequency current. Eddy currents are induced on the surface of the component causing a rapid rise in temperature. This allows a change to austenite in the surface layers of the component. Water jets then cool the steel transforming the austenite to martensite. This leaves the outer surface hard. The frequency of the current determines the depth of heating and the depth of hardening.", marks: 12 },
    ],
