    id: "eng-2011-hl-q6-c", topicId: "eng-1-9", conceptId: "function-any-following-polymer-additives",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2011 HL Q6(c)",
    questionText: "Explain the function of any three of the following polymer additives:\n(i) Plasticiser;\n(ii) Filler;\n(iii) Lubricant;\n(iv) Stabiliser;\n(v) Pigment.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 18,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Plasticiser: Plasticisers are added to polymers to improve their flexibility. They achieve this by altering the forces of attraction between molecules of the polymer.", marks: 18, group: {"claimMax":3,"perOption":6,"options":["Plasticiser: Plasticisers are added to polymers to improve their flexibility. They achieve this by altering the forces of attraction between molecules of the polymer.","Filler: These additives control the mechanical properties, such as material strength, of the polymer. They reduce the amount of expensive polymer used. Fillers such as chalk, wood flour and glass fibre can be used.","Lubricant: Lubricants make the polymer easier to mould. Various types of waxes are used in small amounts for this purpose.","Stabiliser: Help prevent the degradation effects that heat, ultra-violet light and other environmental conditions place on the polymer.","Pigment: Pigments have the function of giving colour to the polymer."]} },
    ],
