    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Engineering 2013 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "eng-2013-hl-q8-a", topicId: "eng-2-15", conceptId: "operation-any-mechanisms-shown",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2013 HL Q8(a)",
    questionText: "Name and describe the operation of any one of the mechanisms shown.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 16,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Universal joint:", marks: 8, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":8,"options":["Universal joint:","Simple helical gear train:"]} },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "The drive rotates the spline shaft of the universal joint which transmits motion through to the output shaft. This allows motion to be transmitted in a line or at an angle. It is commonly used on tractor machinery.", marks: 8, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":8,"options":["The drive rotates the spline shaft of the universal joint which transmits motion through to the output shaft. This allows motion to be transmitted in a line or at an angle. It is commonly used on tractor machinery.","Two shafts are driven in opposite directions by a simple gear train. When there is no difference in gear size, both rotate at the same speed. Speeds can be varied by using different sized gears. The helical teeth on the gears allow a number of teeth on each gear to be in contact at the same time, this gives a smoother and stronger drive. These gear systems may be used on gear driven drills."]} },
    ],
