    section: "A", questionRef: "2015 HL Q1(c)",
    questionText: "Describe the flotation process as a method of ore separation.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 5,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Flotation separation is used for concentrating the metal-bearing mineral in an ore. The metal is ground to a fine powder and mixed with water, frothing reagents, and collecting reagents. When air is blown through the mixture, mineral particles cling to the bubbles, which rise to form a froth on the surface. The waste material settles to the bottom. This froth is skimmed off. This process is used for a number of minerals, especially silver.", marks: 5 },
    ],
