    id: "eng-2021-hl-q1-i", topicId: "eng-1-5", conceptId: "annealed-copper-tubing-typically-used-replace",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2021 HL Q1(i)",
    stem: "Give brief answers to any ten of the following:",
    questionText: "Annealed copper tubing is typically used to replace damaged brake pipes in cars. Briefly describe how copper is annealed.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 5,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Copper is annealed by heating the metal to a red colour (approx. 400°C) and then rapidly cooling it in water. Annealing copper makes it softer and less brittle, which allows you to bend it without breaking it. This malleability allows you to hammer and mould the copper into any shape you wish without cracking the metal.", marks: 5 },
    ],
