    questionText: "Identify and explain the effect of any two of the crystal defects shown opposite.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 8,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A ‐ Vacancy Defect If there is an atom missing from the lattice, the other atoms are forced towards the vacant space.", marks: 8, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":4,"options":["A ‐ Vacancy Defect If there is an atom missing from the lattice, the other atoms are forced towards the vacant space.","B ‐ Interstitial Defect This is where atoms from another element moves into the space between the atoms of the parent metal lattice","C ‐ Substitute Defect If atoms from another element have taken the place of atoms of the parent metal. These atoms may not be the same size and may cause a distortion of the lattice."]} },
    ],
